course: dictionary
lesson: 14180
title: Words about monks and quiet lives
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to a special topic. Monastic comes from monks and nuns, the people who live together in a monastery or convent and give their lives to prayer and work. «The monks followed a monastic routine, rising before dawn to pray.» The clues are monks and rising before dawn, so a monastic routine is strict, quiet and shared.
explain: The word can also describe a way of living with very little in it. «Her bedroom was bare, with one bed and one chair, so it felt monastic.» Here monastic does not mean a monk at all. It means plain, quiet and simple.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Could you say «so it felt plain and simple»? If yes, you have the right idea. Monastic is a more formal word, so you will often meet it in books and history lessons.
fact: Monastic means to do with monks or nuns, and the places they live: monasteries and convents.
fact: Monastic also means very plain, quiet and simple, with few things and little fun.
fact: «Monastic life» is the life of monks or nuns who live together in a religious community.
fact: «Monastic vows» are the promises monks and nuns make, such as poverty, chastity and obedience.
fact: In the Middle Ages, monks copied books by hand, and a «monastic cell» was the small, bare room where a monk lived.
exercise: «The monks followed a monastic routine, rising before dawn to pray.» What does monastic describe? | A fast, noisy party | *A strict, quiet way of life | A sunny beach holiday
exercise: «Her bedroom was bare, with one bed and one chair, so it felt monastic.» What does monastic mean here? | Very cold and damp | Full of bright colours and toys | *Very plain and simple | Covered in gold and jewels
exercise: Monks and nuns live in a place that is linked to the word monastic. Which word names that place? | *Monastery | Market | Museum | Mountain
test: «He chose a monastic life of prayer and work, with no fuss at all.» What does monastic show about his life? | *Plain, quiet and simple | Rich, grand and full of luxury | Noisy, busy and full of parties
test: «The monastic cell had a bed, a stool and a candle.» Which thing is a monastic cell? | *A small, bare room for one monk | A busy shop selling bread | A huge hall full of guests
exam: Which sentence uses monastic correctly? | Monastic jumped over the fence. | *The monastic cell was bare and quiet. | They monastic ran to the shop.
